1065
02:35:28,079 --> 02:35:32,140
If you have polarization, if you have division, those are your problems, and we're just holding up a mirror.

1066
02:35:32,140 --> 02:35:35,980
But the problem is that these companies profit from further division.

1067
02:35:35,980 --> 02:35:42,020
Because imagine there's a Facebook feed, and one Facebook feed gives you an affirmation feed that confirms your view of reality.

1068
02:35:42,180 --> 02:35:45,060
And they have another feed that gives you challenging views of reality.

1069
02:35:45,159 --> 02:35:47,720
Each thing you scroll, it says, well, maybe it's different than how you think.

1070
02:35:48,120 --> 02:35:52,400
Which one of those two feeds is going to be better at keeping your attention, which is their business model?

1071
02:35:52,400 --> 02:35:54,540
The one that affirms your view of reality.

1072
02:35:54,780 --> 02:36:02,420
And so it takes our shared truth and puts it through a paper shredder that puts us into all these narrower and narrower and more extreme views of reality,

1073
02:36:02,420 --> 02:36:04,340
which is really damaging our country.

1074
02:36:04,340 --> 02:36:07,960
Because if we can't agree on what's true, everything else falls apart.

1075
02:36:08,159 --> 02:36:10,460
And this is really the most critical thing in the film.

1076
02:36:10,720 --> 02:36:12,579
You just used the phrase shared truth.

1077
02:36:12,680 --> 02:36:14,020
