1095
02:37:42,636 --> 02:37:47,595
And we are using them in many unconscious ways and just kind of passive ways.

1096
02:37:47,976 --> 02:37:57,595
One of our subjects said they've separated our intention from our attention and kind of hijacked our attention and taken us away from what we are really intending to do.

1097
02:37:58,056 --> 02:38:00,595
I personally have removed myself from these platforms.

1098
02:38:00,595 --> 02:38:05,155
Over the course of making this film, I've completely stopped using social media and I don't feel any loss in life.

1099
02:38:05,235 --> 02:38:06,655
I don't feel disconnected.

1100
02:38:06,855 --> 02:38:12,335
I'm, in fact, engaging with my friends and family through things like FaceTime or Zoom all the more, especially during COVID.

1101
02:38:12,735 --> 02:38:20,095
But I'm not using the platforms that have a different business model, that have ulterior motives, that are trying to manipulate my time and attention.

1102
02:38:20,456 --> 02:38:24,935
There's a line in the film, if you aren't paying for the product, then you are the product.

1103
02:38:24,935 --> 02:38:28,536
That is a real simplification of a really complex set of issues.

1104
02:38:28,536 --> 02:38:32,476
But I find that's the easiest way to think through, is this serving my interests?

1105
02:38:32,595 --> 02:38:33,935
Is this designed for me?

1106
02:38:34,015 --> 02:38:36,115
Is this helping me with what I want to accomplish in life?

1107
02:38:36,415 --> 02:38:37,536
So is there a happy medium?

1108
02:38:37,716 --> 02:38:40,775
Like I would, I can't even tell myself that I'll give up my phones, right?

1109
02:38:40,815 --> 02:38:43,515
Whether we're on Twitter, you know, social media, whatever it is.

1110
02:38:43,876 --> 02:38:44,655
What can we do?

1111
02:38:44,735 --> 02:38:46,876
I mean, you hear about taking the cookies off.

1112
02:38:46,915 --> 02:38:49,175
It just seems like obviously this is way bigger than that.

1113
02:38:49,255 --> 02:38:52,015
Is there any one thing that we can all do to protect ourselves?

1114
02:38:52,015 --> 02:38:59,896
My biggest hope personally is that the film creates a new shared reality about the breakdown of our shared reality.

1115
02:39:00,056 --> 02:39:04,855
And the biggest thing you can do to put reality back together again is to have everybody do a screening of the film.

1116
02:39:04,915 --> 02:39:09,595
We're seeing schools do a whole screening where their whole school comes together or families who can't talk to each other.

1117
02:39:10,015 --> 02:39:13,335
You watch the film together and then you actually open up Facebook on two phones.

1118
02:39:13,335 --> 02:39:14,255
You both use Facebook.

1119
02:39:14,695 --> 02:39:15,796
And you do a reality swap.

1120
02:39:15,796 --> 02:39:24,716
You actually hand them your Facebook feed and then scroll through their feed for a little bit and you'll see, oh, this is why they believe that the things that they're believing because that's the information that they're getting.

1121
02:39:24,815 --> 02:39:27,495
And I think this is so invisible to us because it's so everyday.

1122
02:39:27,695 --> 02:39:33,896
And we're now 10 years into this mass hypnosis psychology experiment where it is fragments our reality into these different things.

1123
02:39:33,935 --> 02:39:35,775
And that's the thing that gives me the most hope.

1124
02:39:35,815 --> 02:39:42,456
And I'm hearing from families and parents saying this is the first time I'm able to talk to my kids about, you know, our use of technology and what's really healthy.

1125
02:39:42,896 --> 02:39:43,716
Let's have the discussion.

1126
02:39:43,775 --> 02:39:44,415
That's fascinating.

